  - ref: module_count_match
    score: 9.0
    verdict: pass
    note: "PDD §4.1 has 6 modules; build has 8. Assessment-only 'Final assessment' module (bonus rule, no deduction) + 'Before you start' baseline module (-1). PDD module content preserved."
  - ref: module_order_match
    score: 10.0
    verdict: pass
    note: "Lessons 1-6 in PDD §4.1 order, bracketed by baseline and gate."
  - ref: assessment_score_wiring
    score: 10.0
    verdict: pass
    note: "connect.assessment final_quiz, user_score = sum(q1_score..q12_score)*100 div 12 (re-read at rev 8, all 12 refs present); 10/12=83.3 passes, 9/12=75 fails vs passing_score 80."
  - ref: content_topic_coverage
    score: 10.0
    verdict: pass
    note: "Every PDD §4.1 outcome present. The rev-7 gap (Module 3 'screen by screen' skipped the Deliver photo-statement screen) is closed: l3_photo_statement sits immediately before l3_photo and teaches read-aloud-first, opt-out by sitting aside, answer Yes only after reading. Call consent taught in Lesson 2 (PDD §4.1 line 'consent to verification calls')."
  - ref: archetype_coherence
    score: 10.0
    verdict: pass
    note: "longitudinal-visits: per-community step state machine taught; scope discipline (no facilitation curriculum) respected."
  - ref: assessment_gating
    score: 9.0
    verdict: pass
    note: "Distinct 6-item non-gating baseline + 12-item gate. Gate covers all 7 PDD §8.3 rules (q1-q7) and every high-consequence operation PDD §4.2 names (register once q8, household count q9, step-completed q11, not-held branch q6, attendance vs participation q2, photo q10, savings amounts q12) — PDD §4.2 coverage requirement fully met by name. Conditional pass (>=80) / fail (<80) labels; fail label lists lessons to re-read, leaks no answers. -1: fixed bank + unlimited retakes (PDD §4.2 acknowledges)."
  - ref: instructional_depth
    score: 9.0
    verdict: pass
    note: "Screen-by-screen teaching, worked counting example (L4), do/don't photo rules with the Deliver reference image (L3), photo-statement procedure now taught (L3), step list and pace (L5), explicit paid/unpaid routing across the two Deliver menus (L3, L6). 2 gate items per taught module. Short of 10: worked examples remain concentrated in L4."
  - ref: assessment_rule_coverage
    score: 9.5
    verdict: pass
    note: "Weighted (11x2 + 9)/(11x2 + 9) = 31/31 = 1.00 over both banks on the rev-7 enumeration; 0 excluded items, 0 items mapping to nothing (start.q5, previously 'rule: none', now keys OP-8). Held at 9.5 not 10: under a defensible extra entry (OP-10 below) the ratio is 31/32 = 0.969 — same band, but the enumeration is the larger error bar."
  - ref: language_conformance
    score: 10.0
    verdict: pass
    note: "English source/default; nya + tum each 196 units, 0 missing, 0 out-of-date, 196 needs-review, 0 ready. Repaired units sampled (tum l3_photo_statement, tum q10 c/d, nya q6 a/c, nya l3_intro/l3_happened/l3_type, nya l6_record_all): origin ai, real target text, menu names aligned to Deliver ('Misonkhano ina'). q10 c/d word ORDER preserved in tum ('pamanyuma' / 'Dankha'). No inline stacking, no language-selector question."




rule_coverage:
  enumeration_source: "PDD §8.3 (7 counter-intuitive rules) + PDD §4.2 operation list + Learn module teaching text (m1-m6) + Deliver blueprint mandatory/validated fields. SAME 20-entry enumeration as the rev-7 verdict, kept deliberately so the repair delta is measured on one denominator."
  counter_intuitive_rules:
    - {id: CI-1,  rule: "a committee meeting is recorded but not paid", taught_in: m6_payment/m3_record, covered_by: final.q1}
    - {id: CI-2,  rule: "people who spoke can never exceed people who attended", taught_in: m4_counts, covered_by: final.q2}
    - {id: CI-3,  rule: "only 3 community meetings per step are paid; the 4th is recorded in full and earns nothing", taught_in: m6_payment, covered_by: final.q3}
    - {id: CI-4,  rule: "the step is read from the record and moves only on 'Yes, completed' at a community meeting", taught_in: m5_steps, covered_by: final.q4}
    - {id: CI-5,  rule: "no savings questions before Step 5 is correct, not a bug", taught_in: m5_steps, covered_by: final.q5}
    - {id: CI-6,  rule: "a planned meeting that did not happen is still recorded with a reason, and not paid", taught_in: m3_record/m6_payment, covered_by: final.q6}
    - {id: CI-7,  rule: "paid per verified meeting (not hours/attendees/households), at most 1 per day", taught_in: m6_payment, covered_by: final.q7}
    - {id: CI-8,  rule: "enrolment household count = ALL households in the community", taught_in: m2_register, covered_by: final.q9}
    - {id: CI-9,  rule: "per-facilitator cap of 21 paid meetings (named number)", taught_in: m6_payment, covered_by: start.q6}
    - {id: CI-10, rule: "a poor location reading is retried at the venue and never blocks payment", taught_in: m3_record, covered_by: start.q3}
    - {id: CI-11, rule: "ANY record may be checked, not only suspicious ones", taught_in: m1_role, covered_by: start.q1}
  counter_intuitive_covered: 11
  operations:
    - {id: OP-1, operation: "register as facilitator once; stop on 'already registered'", taught_in: m2_register, covered_by: start.q2}
    - {id: OP-2, operation: "check the community list; enrol each community once", taught_in: m2_register, covered_by: final.q8}
    - {id: OP-3, operation: "step-completed answer honest; a wrong Yes goes to the supervisor (HQ fix)", taught_in: m5_steps, covered_by: final.q11}
    - {id: OP-4, operation: "count attendance/participation at the meeting, on the day", taught_in: m4_counts, covered_by: start.q4}
    - {id: OP-5, operation: "one wide camera photo of the people during the meeting", taught_in: m3_record, covered_by: final.q10}
    - {id: OP-6, operation: "not saving -> answer No; no amounts (never 0)", taught_in: m5_steps, covered_by: final.q12}
    - {id: OP-7, operation: "route the record to the right Deliver menu: held community meeting -> Community meetings; committee or not-held -> Other meetings", taught_in: m3_record/m6_payment, covered_by: final.q6, status: "RESOLVED by repair (was null at rev 7)"}
    - {id: OP-8, operation: "ask the community contact for consent to verification calls; a No keeps the community in the pilot", taught_in: m2_register, covered_by: start.q5, status: "RESOLVED by repair (was null at rev 7)"}
    - {id: OP-9, operation: "read the photo statement aloud to the group before answering photo_statement_read = Yes", taught_in: m3_record (l3_photo_statement, NEW at rev 8), covered_by: final.q10, status: "RESOLVED by repair (was untaught and untested at rev 7)"}
  operations_covered: 9
  weighted_ratio: 1.00
  items_excluded: 0
  items_mapping_to_nothing: []
  grouping_notes: "not-held reason/new-date folded into CI-6; 'count each speaker once' folded into CI-2; household-count op folded into CI-8."
  sensitivity:
    - "OP-10 (candidate, not in the rev-7 enumeration): one held community meeting per community per day / date later than the last (l3_one_per_day; Deliver validation blocks the form). Untested by any item. Adding it gives 31/32 = 0.969 — same 9-10 band. Low consequence because the Deliver validation itself stops the error at entry; recorded as a residual, not a repair."
    - "OP-5 lost its live-vs-gallery distractor when q10 was re-keyed for OP-9; 'during the meeting' vs 'after' (option b) still tests timing. Camera-only capture is enforced in the Deliver app, so the loss is low-consequence."




items:
  - {id: final.q1,  rule: CI-1, rejectable_distractors: 1, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "b 'not recorded at all' — an untrained worker assumes unpaid work is not logged"}
  - {id: final.q2,  rule: CI-2, rejectable_distractors: 1, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "c 'more than 10 if some spoke more than once' — counting utterances, not people"}
  - {id: final.q3,  rule: CI-3, rejectable_distractors: 0, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "b 'do not record it because it is not paid' — the default expectation for unpaid work"}
  - {id: final.q4,  rule: CI-4, rejectable_distractors: 1, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "a 'choose Step 3 from a list' — how most forms work"}
  - {id: final.q5,  rule: CI-5, rejectable_distractors: 1, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "a 'the app has a problem' — the ordinary reaction to a missing section"}
  - {id: final.q6,  rule: "CI-6 + OP-7", rejectable_distractors: 0, qualifies: true, changed_at_rev: 8, surviving_distractor: "b 'Record it in Community meetings, answer No, and give the reason' — a worker who has not learned the two-menu split records a planned community meeting in the community-meeting form, the natural place; c 'paid because the rain was not your fault' is the fairness intuition"}
  - {id: final.q7,  rule: CI-7, rejectable_distractors: 0, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "b 'both, same amount each' — the per-meeting rule without the daily limit"}
  - {id: final.q8,  rule: OP-2, rejectable_distractors: 1, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "c 'ask the contact person, then enrol' — sounds diligent"}
  - {id: final.q9,  rule: CI-8, rejectable_distractors: 0, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "a '60, the households that come' — the number the worker actually sees"}
  - {id: final.q10, rule: "OP-9 + OP-5", rejectable_distractors: 0, qualifies: true, changed_at_rev: 8, surviving_distractor: "c 'take the wide photo during the meeting, then read the statement' — a worker who knows the photo rules but not the consent order gets the photo right and the sequence wrong; b 'photo of the attendance list after the meeting' is a plausible evidence habit"}
  - {id: final.q11, rule: OP-3, rejectable_distractors: 1, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "c 'answer No next meeting to move the step back' — a plausible in-app self-correction"}
  - {id: final.q12, rule: OP-6, rejectable_distractors: 1, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "a 'enter 0 for each amount' — the flagship blank-not-zero trap"}
  - {id: start.q1,  rule: CI-11, rejectable_distractors: 2, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "a 'only records that look wrong' — how audits are usually imagined"}
  - {id: start.q2,  rule: OP-1, rejectable_distractors: 1, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "d 'finish the form so details are updated'"}
  - {id: start.q3,  rule: CI-10, rejectable_distractors: 1, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "c 'stop; a poor reading means no pay'"}
  - {id: start.q4,  rule: OP-4, rejectable_distractors: 2, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "c 'copy last week's numbers if the same people came'"}
  - {id: start.q5,  rule: OP-8, rejectable_distractors: 0, qualifies: true, changed_at_rev: 8, surviving_distractor: "a 'the community cannot join the pilot' — an untrained worker assumes refusing verification disqualifies; d 'choose a different contact who agrees' reads as problem-solving"}
  - {id: start.q6,  rule: CI-9, rejectable_distractors: 0, qualifies: true, surviving_distractor: "any of 7/14/no-limit — the number cannot be derived"}




prior_repairs_resolution:
  - {repair: "OP-7 Deliver menu routing", resolved: true, evidence: "final.q6 options now differ on menu (Other meetings vs Community meetings) as well as payability; key a; q6_score = if(#form/q6 = 'a',1,0)"}
  - {repair: "OP-8 consent to verification calls", resolved: true, evidence: "start.q5 re-keyed from the consequence-free pace item to the call-consent rule; key b; three plausible distractors"}
  - {repair: "OP-9 photo statement read aloud", resolved: true, evidence: "new Lesson 3 screen l3_photo_statement (839a3331) before l3_photo; final.q10 re-keyed, c vs d differ on order; key d; q10_score = if(#form/q10 = 'd',1,0); nya/tum re-translated (0 out-of-date)"}




repairs: []   # none — and none permitted: the one repair round for this run is spent




residuals:
  - "No further repairs[] round is permitted this run (rubric: cap at one round). Nothing below is a repair work order; these are residuals for a future run."
  - "Fixed 12-item bank with unlimited retakes — a worker can pass by memorising (PDD §4.2; item rotation is an open capability request)."
  - "Rules certified only by the NON-GATING Starting quiz: 21-meeting cap (CI-9), location retry never blocks pay (CI-10), any record may be checked (CI-11), register once (OP-1), count on the day (OP-4), call consent (OP-8). None of these is a PDD §4.2 gate-mandated topic, so no deduction, but a passing certificate does not attest to them."
  - "OP-10 candidate (one held community meeting per community per day) untested; Deliver validation guards it."
  - "q6 and q10 each now carry two rules — one miss costs evidence on two rules; acceptable at a 12-item mandate."




auto_surfaced:
  - severity: WARN
    message: "Fixed 12-item bank with unlimited retakes — a worker can pass by memorising answers (PDD §4.2 acknowledges; item rotation is an open capability request)."
  - severity: WARN
    message: "final.q10 discriminates c vs d on clause ORDER alone ('photo, then statement' vs 'statement, then photo') — long, near-identical options are fragile for a low-literacy reader and in translation. tum was checked and preserves the order ('pamanyuma' / 'Dankha'); the nya rendering and a human reviewer should confirm it reads unambiguously."
  - severity: WARN
    message: "Inflation guard bound: >=2 WARN auto-surfaced -> overall capped at 8.5 (pre-cap 9.50)."
  - severity: INFO
    message: "Prior repairs[] round (graded at rev 7) fully resolved at rev 8: OP-7 (final.q6), OP-8 (start.q5), OP-9 (Lesson 3 l3_photo_statement + final.q10). Rule coverage 0.903 -> 1.00 on the same enumeration."
  - severity: INFO
    message: "Gate certifies every PDD §8.3 rule and every PDD §4.2-named operation. Six taught rules are tested only by the non-gating Starting quiz (CI-9, CI-10, CI-11, OP-1, OP-4, OP-8); Lesson 1 has no gating item. Downgraded from the rev-7 WARN because none is a PDD-declared gate topic."
  - severity: INFO
    message: "Language layer: nya and tum each 196/196 units authored (origin: ai), needs-review 196, ready 0, out-of-date 0, missing 0; English is source and default. needs-review is the normal audit state, not a defect. 8 Connect learn-module names stay single-language by Nova design; 15 media assets shared across locales."
  - severity: INFO
    message: "Defensible structural additions: 'Before you start' baseline module (learn_module only, cannot unlock — ace#1131) and assessment-only 'Final assessment' module."
  - severity: INFO
    message: "FIYP 'Running an Effective Meeting' video absent (open question fiyp-media-assets); Module 3 stands alone as the PDD allows."
  - severity: INFO
    message: "Taught-vs-collectable: the rev-7 gap (Deliver photo_statement_read, untaught in Learn) is closed on the Learn side, as the prior verdict recommended. No new Learn/Deliver disagreement found."




